  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "c1bc72b3-70ea-41a8-8bc7-262000d756b6",
      "question": "Among the 12 most liquid issuers, which had the strongest and weakest returns over the 20 trading sessions ending August 31, 2026, and how did their daily volatility compare?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T04:25:15.075513Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T04:26:32.917295Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Top‑12 most liquid issuers – 20‑session window ending 31 Aug 2026**\n\n| Rank | Asset | 20‑session return | Daily volatility (σ) |\n|------|-------|-------------------|----------------------|\n| **Strongest** | **PEAX** | **+24.74 %** | **2.91 %** |\n| **Weakest**   | **VIAS** | **‑18.78 %** | **2.60 %** |\n\n*Return* is the cumulative adjusted‑close change from the close before the first session to the close of the 20th session. *Volatility* is the daily standard deviation of returns over the same 20 sessions (reported as a fraction; shown here as a percentage).\n\n**Comparison**\n\n- **PEAX** delivered the highest return (+24.7 %) and also showed the slightly higher daily volatility (≈2.9 %).\n- **VIAS** had the lowest return (‑18.8 %) with a modestly lower volatility (≈2.6 %).\n\n**Limitations**\nResults are descriptive historical observations from a synthetic data set and are not investment advice.",
        "citations": []
      },
